{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793739647,"nonce":"zKGLYQkPy4YkUhEnZOKslQqELrg=","title":"Every fem.solve() call re-traces and recompiles a load-path march","message":"A second `fem.solve(...)` on the same fem with the same solver objects spends most of its time tracing and compiling again; the numerical work is a small part. Profile of a repeated call on a small coupled march (staggered displacement/damage, history state, bounds): `pjit cache_miss` -\u003e `_trace_for_jit` and `backend_compile_and_load` dominate, under `history_march._pilot_schedule`. The JAX persistent compilation cache does not change it, and the time barely depends on mesh size.\n\nExpected: a repeated solve reuses the compiled march.","files":null}]}